Subject: [PATCH] build: enable the existing dav1d dependency for FFmpeg AV1

WineDMO already advertises AV1, but the configured native FFmpeg AV1 decoder
requires a hardware accelerator which WineDMO does not provide. GE already
builds and distributes dav1d and lists it in FFMPEG_DEPENDS. Enable its FFmpeg
decoder wrapper rather than adding another library or a Wine decoder picker.
FFmpeg's existing registration order prefers libdav1d over native AV1.

Apply to the GE superproject after SE1's crypto configure patch. This changes
the whole-file Makefile.in postimage: integration requires a NEW candidate's
build-patch provenance, never editing the existing SE1 pin/postimage.

Source-only proposal; not compiled or playback-tested. Existing decoder
thread policy, TLS policy and transport selection are unchanged.
---
diff --git a/Makefile.in b/Makefile.in
--- a/Makefile.in
+++ b/Makefile.in
@@ -353,6 +353,7 @@ FFMPEG_CONFIGURE_ARGS := \
 	--disable-programs \
 	--disable-doc \
 	--disable-inline-asm \
+	--enable-libdav1d \
 	--enable-lzma \
 	--enable-bzlib \
 	--enable-gnutls \
